-**Research Peptide Middleman/Reseller Economics (2026)**
-- Models: (1) white-label dropship — supplier manufactures/labels/ships, you never touch product, ~$1,700-2,000 startup, 1-3 day launch; (2) private-label wholesale — buy bulk, hold inventory, self-fulfill, $8,500-30,000 launch, 60-70% gross; (3) direct manufacturer — MOQ 1,000+, 8-12 wks lead, only at $100K+ MRR.
-- Unit economics example ($80 retail): wholesale $56/48/40/34 at Starter/Growth/Scale tiers (~30/40/50% off retail). Gross margin $24-46/unit. Net after 3.9% processing + white-label: $17-21 (Starter) to $39-43 (Enterprise) = 21-48% net.
-- Realistic net after hidden costs: 19-28% (dropship); 35-40% headline achievable at Scale with repeat customers. Compare: commodity dropship 5-15%, supplements 15-25%.
-- Sample wholesale→MSRP spreads (Premier tier, Jul 2026): NAD+ 1000mg $75→$300 (75%); MOTS-c 10mg $27→$200 (87%); PNC-27 $34→$220 (85%); GLOW blend $82→$250 (67%); BPC-157 10mg $34→$100 (66%); GHK-Cu 50mg $23→$80 (71%); ipamorelin 5mg $15→$35 (59%); CJC-1295 DAC 2mg $25→$55 (55%).
-- Revenue scaling (Growth tier, ~$25/unit net): $10K MRR = 125 units ≈ $3.1K net; $25K = 310 units ≈ $7.8K; $50K = 625 units ≈ $15.6K; $100K = 1,250 units ≈ $31K. Timelines 3-6 mo to 24 mo.
-- Hidden costs that eat margins: high-risk merchant accounts 3.5-5% + 5-10% rolling reserve; chargebacks 1-3% (typical e-comm 0.5%), each $15-25 fee; returns/damage 1%; CAC $30-80 (paid ads restricted on Google/Meta → lean SEO/content); ops overhead 3-8% of revenue.
-- Key structural advantage: paid ads restricted → smaller competitive pool, pricing power. Underserved B2B audience (clinics, labs). Regulatory barrier keeps reseller pool small.
-- Dropship trap: some "white-label wholesale" platforms price at retail, leaving only ~$6.50/vial headroom ($38.50 cost vs $45 retail) — single-digit net, unviable. Real margin requires genuine wholesale (25-50% of retail cost basis).
-- COA/QC: third-party testing $200-800/batch (HPLC+MS); $15-50/COA if add-on. Vendors with per-batch COAs (ISO 17025 blind retest) command premium.
-- Wholesale membership model: e.g. Core $297/mo, Premier $497/mo, zero MOQ, Premier ~20% cheaper per unit. Tier upgrade math: Growth→Scale +$8/unit × 250 = +$2K/mo; Scale→Enterprise +$6/unit × 1,000 = +$6K/mo + net-30.
-- Product mix: sell volume staples (BPC-157, GHK-Cu) + premium complex/long-chain peptides (retatrutide, tirzepatide, NAD+ 1000mg) where margins run 70-87%. Sequence length adds 8-12%/aa; ≥98% purity adds 15-20% vs 95%.
-- Legal/gray-market caveat: sold "for research use only, not for human consumption." Real consumer demand is largely self-administration of unapproved drugs — FDA warning letters, CBP seizures, 12-peptide Category 2 removal (Apr 2026), PCAC review Jul 2026, payment processor risk. Legal risk is the main unbudgetable variable; most operators are 1 FDA enforcement action from extinction.
