-**06:21 - "Idea Relay" Marketplace: alternative to Kickstarter/Patreon**
-- Creators post a concept or prototype they CAN'T finish (missing skills/time/funds/resources/tools, or lost drive) — explicitly NOT a funding ask.
-- The idea itself is the asset; value is in its lineage, not a solo creator.
-- Backend overlap engine finds related posted projects and evaluates best path forward (merge / handoff / consolidate), with transparent match logic exposed.
-- Blockchain ledger anchors provenance: original idea hash + signed contribution transactions forming a lineage DAG (who was first is provable; contributions = value-add layers).
-- Every contribution earns a weighted "value-added" score (downstream builds, adoption, endorsements); displayed as public reputation.
-- Downstream monetization: project "graduates" to funding/subscription; a royalty pool is split by score weights across the whole lineage, originator holds a reserved floor share.
-- Design pillars: posting flow with declared blockers, matchmaking, provenance DAG, scoring, royalty split, anti-abuse (fork spam / squatting / Sybil), legal wrapper (SPV/LLC/DAO + smart contracts).
-- Key open problems: objectively measuring contribution value, license defaults for forks, cold start, securities-law risk on revenue-sharing tokens.
