-**MDM-Locked MacBook "Asahi Linux + Local LLM" Flip Idea — Reality Check**
-- Concept: buy MDM-locked high-end MacBook Pros at ~half price, install Asahi Linux, skin it to look/feel like macOS, preload a local LLM stack (Ollama/llama.cpp), resell at a premium.
-- Fatal flaw: MDM-locked units are almost always stolen/diverted enterprise or school property; the lock is registered to the original org and cannot be cleared by a reseller. Buying them knowingly to flip = receiving stolen property. The "half price" IS the stolen risk priced in.
-- Asahi runs on MDM-locked hardware (bypasses macOS activation) but the serial stays hot: blacklisted, no Apple support, org can remote-lock/wipe. The lock never goes away.
-- macOS-skin + Linux: refund magnet — buyers who wanted macOS get a themed Linux box. LLM premium is thin; buyers can install the same OSS stack in an afternoon.
-- Legitimate version: buy MDM-cleared / asset-removed Macs from certified refurbishers (proof of owner disposal on file) and sell "Asahi Linux + local LLM setup" as a service on top of honest refurb pricing. Thinner margin, real repeatable business.
-- Market baseline (used MacBook Pro 13" M2, 2026): 8GB/256GB ~$595–650; 8GB/512GB ~$618–777; 16GB/512GB ~$700–1,170 refurb; 14"/16" M2 Pro/Max sell $1,100–2,400. Asahi Linux preinstalled doesn't create a separate market segment — price is set by hardware config.
