-**Solar e-Bike Towed Camper Trailer — Build Plan (Physics + Phases)**
-- Goal: teardrop camper towed by Onyx RCR-class e-bike, 70 mph via 2x trailer hub motors, solar on roof.
-- Physics reality: 70 mph needs ~15 kW aero (Cd .45 teardrop) to ~24 kW (boxy); +rolling/losses → 17–25 kW sustained. Trailer motors do the work; solar (500–600 W roof, ~3 kWh/day) = campsite power + ~20–30 mi/day at 25 mph, NOT highway speed. 20 kWh pack → ~50–60 mi at 70 mph.
-- Build phases: 0) legal (MC class + trailer reg) & weight target <400 kg; 1) custom lightweight teardrop, long drawbar tongue, 10–15% tongue weight, torsion axle, 17" MC-rated tires, 70 mph bearings; 2) 2x 10 kW hub motors (QS 273 class) + dual FOC controllers, differential torque control for sway damping, throttle split from bike; 3) 96V ~20 kWh NMC/LFP (~120 kg), dual packs, BMS/contactors/fusing, fire-rated vented battery bay sealed from living space; 4) 600 W rigid + air gap + MPPT, optional fold-out wings ~1.2 kW; 5) regen + mech disc brakes, lights/reflectors, sway hitch, thermal limiting; 6) incremental stability/braking tests 30→50 mph before 70.
-- Budget: trailer $4–8k, drive $2.5–4k, battery $3–6k, solar $1–3k, chassis $1.5–3k, integration $1–2k → ~$14–26k.
-- Key risks: trailer sway at speed (mitigate via torque-vectoring), hub motor thermal limits, battery fire in sleeping space, legal classification.
